1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,611
What if everything around
you could become a 3D model?

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:06,691
Not in a studio. Right where you stand.

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:11,102
Put on a headset, and the
world stops being a picture.

4
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:15,496
It becomes something you can
point at, take, and build with.

5
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:18,987
See that car? Point at it.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,600
The AI sees it, outlines it, and
rebuilds it in three dimensions.

7
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:29,250
Now imagine doing that to
power a whole village.

8
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:35,524
This is Mitsinjo Grid VR: a solar
village twin for off-grid Madagascar,

9
00:00:35,394 --> 00:00:38,794
running in the browser with
Meta's WebXR emulator.

10
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:42,816
On the Village page, I enter
VR immersion and walk around.

11
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:46,086
One trigger on the floating
button analyses the current view.

12
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:50,800
Muse Spark detects every
object, SAM outlines it.

13
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:55,061
Each detection becomes a
hologram. I aim the laser…

14
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:58,430
…and shoot the object I want.

15
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,657
The app asks: extract it in 3D? Yes.

16
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,800
I step into the 3D studio.
Muse Image draws its 2D views:

17
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,578
front, sides, back and top.

18
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:19,749
If one view is wrong, I just ask the AI chat,
by voice or keyboard, and it redraws it.

19
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:24,600
I check every view and validate. Nothing
is built until a human says yes.

20
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,600
From the validated views, the 3D
model is built, piece by piece.

21
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:34,522
In the 3D lab I turn it, shoot a
piece to select it, resize it.

22
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:39,149
Every edit goes live to the
village and to the page.

23
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:44,221
Then I aim at the village
table and place it.

24
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:49,371
A pole and a cable connect
it to its feeder line.

25
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:56,600
Insert into simulation: the energy
engine recomputes every strategy.

26
00:01:56,400 --> 00:02:00,708
Go to the simulation. Now I
am standing inside the grid.

27
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:06,200
I walk the village at human scale. Walls
stop me, the ground follows my feet.

28
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:11,841
Labels, a live map, and every line
carrying the engine's simulated power.

29
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:17,200
I aim at a building: a hologram panel
shows what the engine serves it.

30
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:21,444
Minus half a kilowatt. The
whole village sees the change.

31
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:26,879
I walk in: the lights inside glow
with the power it really gets.

32
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:33,094
At the dispatcher, a mixing desk.
Start the battery and dispatch.

33
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:38,000
One fader per sector. Slide, release,
and the energy flows change.

34
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:42,200
Try to cut the clinic? Refused. The
village constitution protects it.

35
00:02:41,940 --> 00:02:46,521
Mitsinjo Grid VR. Point at the
world. Build it. Power it.

36
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:51,829
Every number comes from the engine.
Every action stays in human hands.
